			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> i would say no actually, same with something like webc (for is-land in particular you have the luck of `is-land` seemingly still being available as a non-scoped package name! could use that and move it under your personal account)</p>",
