			"date": "2025-02-27T20:42:27.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Silly question (out of curiosity, not anything I am dead-set on figuring out): for the Google Dev site, the favicon is evenly (ish) spread across 4 colours, but the output is yellow. I didn't look too much at the code (sorry) but is there a magic thing that determines which hue \"wins\"?</p><p>Also, gotta say this is very cool! It fits neatly in the \"Whimsy\" and \"Surprise &amp; Delight\" Venn diagram. (as overused as that second term may be these days 😅)</p>",
